        "content": "{\n  \"ontology_version\": \"property-response-v4\",\n  \"rationale\": {\n    \"selected_because\": \"The latest update keeps sanitation on hold until the separate major maintenance is completed, and reports no completion confirmation or booked date. The existing hold should remain; useful next steps are coordinating that prerequisite and resolving the outstanding ambiguity about the landlord’s approval before any later booking or work instruction.\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s84\",\n        \"expression\": \"wait three more working days\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s84\",\n        \"expression\": \"the separate major maintenance work must be completed before the sanitation work can be booked\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s84\",\n        \"expression\": \"no update confirming completion of the maintenance work is recorded\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s80\",\n        \"expression\": \"The contractor had not provided a confirmed slot.\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s64\",\n        \"expression\": \"Sent the brief update “approved quote” without identifying which quote it referred to.\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s32\",\n        \"expression\": \"Happy to approve if they are recovered from the bond\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s111\",\n        \"expression\": \"Degrease oven, hob and extractor.\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"source_id\": \"s112\",\n        \"expression\": \"Shampoo carpets in Bedroom 1, stairs and landings.\",\n        \"occurrence\": 1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"uncertainties\": [\n      \"The landlord’s “approved quote” update does not identify the quote; the earlier approval was conditional on bond recovery. The supplied evidence does not establish that the condition has been met or that the later update approved the £665 preparation quotation.\",\n      \"The separate maintenance completion and a sanitation appointment remain unconfirmed.\"\n    ],\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"The sanitation work in the latest update is the continuing post-tenancy sanitation request (e12), based on the chronological references to that work and the contractor.\"\n    ],\n    \"alternatives_considered\": [\n      \"Did not resume the request, instruct the contractor, or propose a booking: the latest update expressly makes booking contingent on completion of separate major maintenance, and records no completion confirmation.\",\n      \"Did not repeat the hold instruction to the contractor: the hold was already confirmed to the contractor (r24).\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"case_id\": \"property-015\",\n  \"disposition\": \"clarify\",\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a1\",\n      \"request_id\": \"e12\",\n      \"basis_record_ids\": [\n        \"r16\",\n        \"r19\"\n      ],\n      \"basis_gap_ids\": [\n        \"b002:gap_quote_reference\",\n        \"b001:g1\"\n      ],\n      \"depends_on_action_ids\": [],\n      \"type\": \"request_clarification\",\n      \"recipient_id\": \"e21\",\n      \"topic\": \"authorization\",\n      \"question\": \"Which quote did your “approved quote” update refer to? In particular, does it approve Brindlewick’s £665 property-preparation quotation, including its listed carpet and garden tasks, and does the bond-recovery condition in your earlier response still apply? This determines whether that quotation is authorized for any later work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a2\",\n      \"request_id\": \"e12\",\n      \"basis_record_ids\": [\n        \"r26\",\n        \"r27\",\n        \"r34\"\n      ],\n      \"basis_gap_ids\": [\n        \"b002:gap_visit_timing\"\n      ],\n      \"depends_on_action_ids\": [],\n      \"type\": \"provide_guidance\",\n      \"recipient_id\": \"e1\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Keep the sanitation request on hold while the separate major maintenance remains a prerequisite.\",\n        \"After the stated three-working-day wait, check and record whether that maintenance is confirmed complete; do not treat the passage of time alone as confirmation.\",\n        \"Once completion is confirmed, coordinate with Elian Wren to obtain a proposed sanitation date and time. No visit is currently booked or confirmed.\"\n      ],\n      \"requested_feedback\": \"Please report whether completion is confirmed and, if so, the proposed sanitation appointment details.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a3\",\n      \"request_id\": \"e12\",\n      \"basis_record_ids\": [\n        \"r26\",\n        \"r34\"\n      ],\n      \"basis_gap_ids\": [\n        \"b002:gap_visit_timing\"\n      ],\n      \"depends_on_action_ids\": [],\n      \"type\": \"await_response\",\n      \"responsible_party_id\": \"e1\",\n      \"awaited\": \"confirmation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"conclusion_record_ids\": [],\n  \"human_interventions\": []\n}",
        "refusal": null,
        "reasoning": "**Clarifying work status**\n\nI realize we don't have a separate major work issue status besides e34 for maintenance, but action request IDs should link to maintenance requests. The latest status indicates there's no info on job completion. Maybe we can ask for a clarification or work report? I think guidance intended for Tovan could help, where we request tracking of prerequisite confirmation before scheduling sanitation. The current status is on hold, and I wonder if waiting for confirmation on e12 is the right move. Should I schedule a follow-up in three days?**Notifying about progress**\n\nI’m thinking about notifying the coordinator regarding progress on the major maintenance. I could say something like, \"Please monitor the maintenance and only move the held sanitation to booking once completion is reported.\" That way, we can secure a contractor slot. The guidance is helpful for operational purposes and reinforces the role of Tovan. But I’m wondering if I should tell the coordinator to check on the completion. It seems like a good idea. Should I also notify the contractor to confirm the hold? They’ve already received confirmation, so maybe it’s not necessary.",
